# Auto commit & push to main

When finished product/app work is ready in this repo, **commit and push to `origin/main` without waiting to be asked**.

## Do
- Commit relevant tracked/new app source (and related tests, migrations, project rules).
- Prefer one or two why-focused commits (HEREDOC messages), then `git push origin main` (or the branch that tracks main).
- Confirm local main matches `origin/main` after push.

## Do not
- Force push, amend unless amend rules are fully met, or skip hooks.
- Commit secrets (`.env`, credentials) or junk: pitch decks, YC/application drafts, `*.prompt.md`, zips, business-plan docs, backups, unrelated marketing PDFs.
- Push if the user explicitly said not to, or if the only changes are dangerous/secrets.

## Default
Treat "yes push everything to main automatically every time" as standing preference for this user/repo.
